{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "id": "e-figure",
  "lexicon": "gkv",
  "number": 1497,
  "kind": "word",
  "headword": "figure",
  "ipa": [
    "ˈfɪɡə(r)"
  ],
  "levelMark": true,
  "senses": [
    {
      "pos": "n.",
      "zh": "数字；外形，轮廓；人影；人物"
    },
    {
      "pos": "vt.",
      "zh": "计算；用图表（或图画）描绘；描述；塑造"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Children are afraid of the stone "
        },
        {
          "t": "underline",
          "v": "figures"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " in the temple which look so frightening."
        }
      ],
      "zh": "孩子们害怕寺庙里那些看起来很可怕的石像。"
    },
    {
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Have you "
        },
        {
          "t": "underline",
          "v": "figured"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " out how much the journey to New Zealand will cost?"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "你算出这次去新西兰旅游要花多少钱吗？"
    }
  ],
  "phrases": [
    {
      "en": "figure out",
      "zh": "计算出；解决"
    }
  ],
  "compare": [
    {
      "words": "figure, form, shape",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "这三个词的一般含义为“形状”或“外形”。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "figure"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 表示隐约可见的“人影”或“物影”，以及几何“图形”、人体“外形”、引人注目的“人物或塑像”等。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "In the torchlight he caught sight of a "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "figure"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " whom he immediately recognised as Bill Wilkins, our local grocer. 他在手电筒的光下看到一个人影，立刻认出这个人是本地杂货商比尔·威尔金斯。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "form"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 最普通、使用范围最广、含义最多，哲学上讲的“形态”，文艺上讲的“体裁”，雕刻艺术上讲的“形状”，以及普通的含义“方式”或“形式”等，它都可以表示。此外，form 也可以表示人或动物的“体形”“外形”。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Strange "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "forms"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " stand in gardens, and outside buildings and shops. 花园里、建筑物和商店外面竖立着奇形怪状的雕塑形体。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "shape"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 表示“外形”或“形状”以及“（人物）体形”。其内涵是：外形之下具有实体。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "The bridge is so long that the "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "shape"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " of the Earth had to be taken into account by its designer. 桥身如此长，以至于它的设计师不得不考虑地球的形状。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Before long, biscuits of all "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "shapes"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " and sizes began arriving at the factory. 不久，大大小小各种形状的饼干开始送到这家工厂。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "另外，这三个词的含义差异还可以从它们表示的人体外形的差异上来进行辨析。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "form"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 所指的“人体外形”在意义上很含糊，只是能够认出，但未必看得仔细或看得清楚。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c11",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "What he saw seemed to have the "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "form"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " of a man. 他所看到的似乎是一个男子的身影。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c12",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "entertainment in the "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "form"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " of opera 以戏剧形式的娱乐（强调可以认出的形式或形状）"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c13",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "in "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "form"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 在形式上，在外形上（用于抽象的、无实体的事物）"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c14",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "figure"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 在表示“人体外形”时通常因黑暗而看不清楚，即“人影”，而且只强调身体的轮廓。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c15",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "She has a very good "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "figure"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": ". 她的体形很优美。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c16",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "to cut a piece of paper in the "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "figure"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " of a triangle 把纸剪成三角形（强调轮廓）"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c17",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "shape"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 包括躯体轮廓也包含有血有肉的身体。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c18",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "to form a mass of clay in the "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "shape"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " of a man 把一堆黏土塑造成男人的形状（强调实体）"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c19",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "in "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "shape"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 在外形上（用于具有实体的事物）"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
